/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - At saturation, liquid and vapour coexist.
   - Psat is saturation pressure (Pa), T is absolute temperature (K), ΔH is latent heat (J/mol), and ΔV = Vg − Vl is molar volume change (m³/mol).
   - Derivation: along the coexistence curve Gl = Gg, so a small step keeps dGl = dGg: −Sl dT + Vl dP = −Sg dT + Vg dP.
   - A large ΔH makes the curve steep.
   - For liquid–vapour saturation away from the critical point, Vg ≫ Vl, so ΔV ≈ Vg.
   - Psat is saturation pressure, T is absolute temperature, ΔH is molar latent heat, and R is the gas constant.
   - Integrate from (P1, T1) to (P2, T2).
   - P1 and P2 are saturation pressures in the same unit, T1 and T2 are in K, ΔH is in J/mol, and R = 8.314 J mol⁻¹ K⁻¹.
   - Equivalently, ln Psat = A − ΔH/(R T).
*/
